From: SoundTap <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: davinci-mcasp: let DIT run at 46875 Hz, labelled 48 kHz

The SoundTouch 300 sends its audio to the soundbar's DSP over S/PDIF from
McASP0, clocked from AUXCLK: 24 MHz / 2 / 2 = 6 MHz of biphase clock, 128 x
46875 Hz. That is the only rate the link can make, it is where stock runs the
same registers (read off a running stock unit on 2026-11-06), and the machine
driver constrains the link to it.

mcasp_dit_hw_param() picks the channel-status sample-rate code from a list of
standard rates and refuses anything else, so every open of the ST300's card
failed:

  davinci-mcasp 48038000.mcasp: unsupported sampling rate: 46875

46875 Hz is 48 kHz running 2.3 % slow, well inside what an S/PDIF receiver's
PLL follows, so label it 48 kHz.

--- a/sound/soc/ti/davinci-mcasp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/davinci-mcasp.c
@@ -1106,6 +1106,12 @@
 	case 44100:
 		cs_bytes[3] |= IEC958_AES3_CON_FS_44100;
 		break;
+	/*
+	 * 46875 Hz: 24 MHz AUXCLK / 2 / 2 / 128, the one rate an S/PDIF link
+	 * clocked from AUXCLK reaches. It is 48 kHz running 2.3 % slow, so it
+	 * carries the 48 kHz code.
+	 */
+	case 46875:
 	case 48000:
 		cs_bytes[3] |= IEC958_AES3_CON_FS_48000;
 		break;
